<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.1" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="42349-1" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Reason for referral (narrative)"/>
    <title>Reason for Referral</title>
    <text><paragraph>Please evaluate and advise on exudative age-related macular degeneration, left eye, with active choroidal neovascularization and nonexudative age-related macular degeneration, right eye, intermediate dry stage. [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Same-week ophthalmology consultation for new distortion and reduced acuity in the left eye, with OCT and fluorescein or OCT angiography as needed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Seen in ophthalmology consultation at the request of Wendell Ashby, MD. [S]</paragraph><list><item>Afraid of losing the central vision she needs to paint. [S]</item><item>Wants to keep living alone and driving to her studio. [S]</item></list><paragraph>Historical basis. These claims are historical evidence, not findings from a modern examination.</paragraph><list><item>Georgia Totto O&apos;Keeffe was born on November 15, 1887, to Francis Calyxtus O&apos;Keeffe and Ida Totto O&apos;Keeffe at the family dairy farm near Sun Prairie, Wisconsin, the second of seven children. [D]</item><item>O&apos;Keeffe&apos;s mother died in Charlottesville, Virginia, in May 1916, and her father died in Petersburg, Virginia, in November 1918. [D]</item><item>In 1927 O&apos;Keeffe was admitted twice to Mount Sinai Hospital in New York for surgery to remove benign breast cysts. [D]</item><item>In February 1933 O&apos;Keeffe was admitted to Doctor&apos;s Hospital in New York, suffering from psychoneurosis, and recuperated in Bermuda in March and April. [D]</item><item>O&apos;Keeffe&apos;s eyesight began to fail in 1968. [D]</item><item>The first signs of O&apos;Keeffe&apos;s macular degeneration may have appeared as early as 1964. [R]</item></list><paragraph>4 later historical claims are omitted because they describe events after the index age. See the teaching note.</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

